<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<office:document
	xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0"
	xmlns:style="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:style:1.0"
	xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0"
	xmlns:table="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:table:1.0"
	xmlns:fo="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:xsl-fo-compatible:1.0"
	xmlns:number="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:datastyle:1.0"
	office:version="1.3"
	office:mimetype="application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.spreadsheet">

	<office:automatic-styles>
		<style:style style:name="coNarrow" style:family="table-column">
			<style:table-column-properties style:column-width="0.9in"/>
		</style:style>
		<style:style style:name="coMed" style:family="table-column">
			<style:table-column-properties style:column-width="1.7in"/>
		</style:style>
		<style:style style:name="coWide" style:family="table-column">
			<style:table-column-properties style:column-width="6.5in"/>
		</style:style>
		<style:style style:name="ceHead" style:family="table-cell">
			<style:table-cell-properties fo:background-color="#dddddd"/>
			<style:text-properties fo:font-weight="bold"/>
		</style:style>
		<style:style style:name="ceWrap" style:family="table-cell">
			<style:table-cell-properties fo:wrap-option="wrap" style:vertical-align="top"/>
		</style:style>
		<style:style style:name="ceBad" style:family="table-cell">
			<style:table-cell-properties fo:background-color="#ffdddd"/>
		</style:style>
	</office:automatic-styles>

	<office:body>
	<office:spreadsheet>

	<!-- ============================== Session ============================== -->
	<table:table table:name="Session">
		<table:table-column table:style-name="coMed"/>
		<table:table-column table:style-name="coWide"/>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceHead" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Field</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceHead" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Value</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Date</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>2026-08-14</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Times in this file</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>UTC, matching the results store. Local was UTC-4, so 17:23Z is 13:23 local.</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Purpose</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Fill the Windows rows of the README shootout table (conhost, Windows Terminal, MobaXterm), which have never been measured because the two rigs need a Linux display.</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Outcome</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Nothing published. The figures are real and repeatable but not comparable with the existing rows, for the reasons on the Validity sheet. Numbers kept here so a later pass on comparable hardware has a baseline to check itself against.</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Raw records</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>%LOCALAPPDATA%\silkterm-bench\results.jsonl (31 records, including the discarded and exploratory ones)</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row/>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceHead" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Measured on</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceHead" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Reference rig the table was built on</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Lenovo 20Y1S00C00 (laptop, bare metal)</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>b23 (desktop)</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, 8C/16T, mobile</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>AMD Ryzen 9 3950X, desktop</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>AMD Radeon Pro, integrated</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>GeForce RTX 3060 Ti, discrete</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>37.7 GiB</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>not recorded here</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200, Python 3.14.7</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Linux, headless Wayland compositor on the discrete GPU</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
		<table:table-row/>
		<table:table-row>
			<table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Note</text:p></table:table-cell>
			<table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"><text:p>README footnote 9 anticipates the Windows rows coming from a VM on the b23 host with a passed-through RTX 2060. That is not this machine. This is a different physical laptop with integrated graphics, which is the single biggest reason the figures below cannot be published beside the Linux rows.</text:p></table:table-cell>
		</table:table-row>
	</table:table>

